u(100,'A/Lattices/Valued/Equivariant.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/Involution.lean','This bundle needs primitivity/nonsingularity of invariants and perpendicular coinvariants, an index bound and p-elementarity for arbitrary prime-order action. Involution-only or constructor-only data is insufficient.','primitivegluing')
a(101,'A/Lattices/Valued/Gluing.lean :: Overlattice; A/Lattices/Valued/ScaleAndEvenness.lean :: IsEven','For a nondegenerate integral lattice, Overlattice is an integral intermediate carrier between L and its metric dual; finite index follows from the finite discriminant setting. The source quadratic-overlattice refinement is exactly the IsEven condition on the restricted form.','gluing')
t(102,'T/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/Overlattice/Isotropic.lean :: integralIntermediateCarrierOrderIsoIsotropicSubgroup, evenIntermediateCarrierOrderIsoIsotropicSubgroup; T/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/Overlattice/OrthogonalQuotient/Bilinear.lean :: IntermediateCarrier.discriminantBilinearOrthogonalQuotientIsometry; T/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/Overlattice/OrthogonalQuotient/Quadratic.lean :: IntermediateCarrier.discriminantOrthogonalQuotientIsometry; T/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/Overlattice/Dual.lean :: IntermediateCarrier.dual_eq_self_iff_isLagrangian','Full isotropic-subgroup correspondence as an order isomorphism, discriminant isometry A_M≃H-perp/H and unimodularity iff self-orthogonal subgroup. The quadratic version uses half norm in Q/Z and even subgroups/lattices. All statements assume the original lattice nondegenerate.','gluing')
u(103,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean; T/LinearAlgebra/FiniteBilinearModule/KleinFour.lean','No complete enumeration of the three bilinear-isotropic lines of U(2), two quadratic-isotropic lines and the two specified even overlattices was identified.','gluing')
u(104,'T/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/RootLattice/D8Plus/Isometry.lean','D8+≃E8 is a candidate, but the source bundle additionally uses the particular binary isotropic code in A_(Z8(2)) and a uniqueness assertion. The specific glue construction and uniqueness are not supplied by the isometry alone.','roots')
u(105,'A/Lattices/Valued/EvenGluing.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/DiscriminantQuadratic.lean','Anti-isometry structures and glue constructors assume the discriminant anti-isometry. They do not prove it from primitively embedded orthogonal complements in a unimodular lattice.','primitivegluing')
t(106,'T/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/Overlattice/Naturality.lean :: Isometry.discriminantSubgroup_intermediateCarrierEquiv, Isometry.intermediateCarrierEquiv_intermediateCarrierOfDiscriminantSubgroup, Isometry.toIntegralLatticeIsometry','The order-isomorphism transport identifies the transported overlattice with the preimage of the transported discriminant subgroup, and constructs the restricting lattice isometry. Equality of the subgroup is equivalent to equality of its preimage by the established order isomorphism. This supplies both directions of the extension criterion.','gluing')
u(107,'A/Lattices/Valued/EvenGluing.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean','No general primitive embedding S into U^a with perpendicular -S⊕U^(a-rank S) and all source rank/parity assumptions was identified.','primitivegluing')
a(108,'A/Lattices/Valued/BaseChange.lean :: baseChangeFiniteIntegral, baseChangeIntegral_pairing_tmul','Specializing finite integral scalar extension to Z -> Z_p gives L_p = L tensor Z_p and the displayed p-adic bilinear extension on pure tensors.','local')
u(109,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalInvariants.lean :: FieldSquareClass, UnitSquareClass','The local lattice determinant retains its valuation and is taken modulo squares of units, whereas FieldSquareClass discards even valuation. The exact quotient/pair encoding for arbitrary nonzero determinant has not been identified.','local')
a(110,'A/Lattices/Valued/MetricDual.lean :: IsFractionFieldNondegenerate, IsUnimodular','Specialize the integral pairing to Z_p; rational nondegeneracy and integral unimodularity remain distinct. Nonzero/unit Gram determinant criteria are the respective ones.','local')
a(111,'A/Lattices/Valued/Discriminant.lean :: discriminantGroup, FractionValueQuotient, discriminantBilinMap; A/Lattices/Valued/DiscriminantQuadratic.lean :: evenDiscriminantQuadraticMap, doubleValueEquiv','Specializing to the p-adic integer ring gives the bilinear discriminant form. For a quadratic lattice the project stores twice the source quadratic value in the double quotient; doubleValueEquiv is multiplication by two and identifies that convention with the source quotient-valued quadratic discriminant form.','local')
u(112,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalGlobal.lean; P/NumberTheory/NumberField/Completion/FinitePlace.lean','The source also introduces the places of a general number field, not merely the primes and real place of Q. Verify the unified finite/infinite place owner and notation before claiming this bundle.','local')
a(113,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalGlobal.lean :: SameGenus','SameGenus quantifies integral isometry over all Z_p and real isometry, not just equality of rational forms over Q_p.','local')
u(114,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalGlobal.lean; X/Hanke/Lean/QuadraticForms/LocalGlobalHassePrinciple.lean','The local-global rational isometry consequence and the existence of distinct global integral classes in one genus are both required. Hanke LocalGlobalHassePrinciple is an empty imports/comments file; RatfuncWitt uses a different field. Neither supplies Hasse–Minkowski over Q.','hasse')
u(115,'A/Lattices/Valued/GenusInvariants.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/BaseChange.lean','Need all local nondegeneracy/unimodularity tests and localization of discriminant. Global unimodularity is equivalent to unimodularity at every prime, not at one chosen prime. The individual base-change construction is insufficient.','local')
u(116,'A/Lattices/Valued/SmithNormalForm.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/GenusInvariants.lean','No complete signed-determinant reconstruction from the sign and the product of local discriminant orders was identified.','local')
u(117,'A/Lattices/Valued/GenusInvariants.lean :: determinant_eq_of_sameGenus','Signed determinant invariance exists. The entire source unit also includes parity invariance, which needs the integral two-adic test; do not count the determinant theorem as the pair of invariants.','local')
u(118,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalInvariants.lean','The specified determinant and local unit-square-class computations at 2,3,7 were not found as a verified Lean example.','local')
u(119,'A/Lattices/Valued/Discriminant.lean; T/LinearAlgebra/FiniteBilinearModule/Primary/Decomposition.lean','Primary decomposition of an abstract finite form does not identify it with the discriminant of the p-adic base-changed lattice. That localization comparison for both b and q is the required claim.','local')
u(120,'A/Lattices/Valued/GenusInvariants.lean','Genus invariance of numerical determinant/signature is weaker than an isometry of the entire finite discriminant form; no complete globalization of all primary form isometries was identified.','local')
u(121,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalInvariants.lean; T/LinearAlgebra/FiniteBilinearModule/Cyclic.lean','The odd-p integral rank-one classification must include the two unit square classes and the resulting cyclic discriminant forms. A generic unit square-class quotient or a specified cyclic form is not the classification.','local')
u(122,'T/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/RankOne.lean; T/LinearAlgebra/FiniteBilinearModule/Cyclic.lean','The source compares p-adic rank-one quadratic isometry classes by unit square classes. TauCeti rankOne is an even Z-lattice calculation, not this local classification.','local')
u(123,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalInvariants.lean','The four unit square classes ±1,±3 over Z_2 and their completeness/distinctness need an exact theorem, not merely the quotient type.','dyadic')
u(124,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalInvariants.lean; T/LinearAlgebra/FiniteBilinearModule/Cyclic.lean','The complete dyadic rank-one classification and special distinctions for small exponents k were not identified.','dyadic')
a(125,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean :: hyperbolicPlane, hyperbolicPlane_gramMatrix; A/Lattices/Valued/BaseChange.lean :: baseChangeIntegral, baseChangeIntegral_pairing_tmul; A/Lattices/Valued/Constructions.lean :: scaleLattice','Base-change the integral hyperbolic plane to the p-adic integers and scale its pairing by p^k; the standard-basis Gram matrix is then exactly the displayed U_k matrix.','dyadic')
u(126,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/Discriminant.lean','Need the full U_k determinant, quadratic polar convention and explicit finite discriminant pairings at every exponent. Generic constructors do not prove the computation.','dyadic')
u(127,'T/LinearAlgebra/FiniteBilinearModule/KleinFour.lean','The source u_k family has exponent 2^k for arbitrary k; the Klein-four model only covers exponent two. No all-k canonical finite quadratic owner was identified.','dyadic')
u(128,'T/LinearAlgebra/FiniteBilinearModule/KleinFour.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean','The all-k V_k matrix, determinant, discriminant refinement and u_1/v_1 bilinear-equal but quadratic-distinct comparison constitute one bundle, not a rank-two constructor.','dyadic')
u(129,'T/LinearAlgebra/FiniteBilinearModule/KleinFour.lean','A v_1 model is not the source arbitrary-exponent v_k finite quadratic family.','dyadic')
u(130,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalGlobal.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/GenusInvariants.lean','Nikulin genus classification by signature and the entire finite quadratic discriminant form is not implied by numerical genus invariants or the definition of SameGenus.','nikulin')
u(131,'A/Lattices/Valued/Signature.lean; T/LinearAlgebra/FiniteBilinearModule/Quadratic.lean','The mod-eight signature invariant of a finite quadratic form requires existence of an even realization and independence from the realization, not simply reducing one lattice signature modulo eight.','nikulin')
u(132,'A/Lattices/Valued/EvenGluing.lean','No full even-lattice realization theorem with the stated signature, mod-eight compatibility and strict rank/length inequality was found.','nikulin')
u(133,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean','The E7 lattice and cyclic discriminant carrier exist, but the specified finite quadratic value -3/4 and its tau_8=1 realization comparison were not identified as a complete example.','nikulin')
u(134,'A/Lattices/Valued/ClassFiniteness.lean','The inspected finiteness results concern positive definite lattices. The source Eisenstein–Hermite theorem covers all nondegenerate integral lattices, including indefinite ones, of fixed rank and bounded absolute discriminant.','classfinite')
u(135,'A/Lattices/Valued/Reduction.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/ClassFiniteness.lean','The source minimum uses the absolute norm of every nonzero vector and is zero for an isotropic vector. Positive-definite shortest-vector minima are not this definition on arbitrary nondegenerate lattices.','hermite')
u(136,'A/Lattices/Valued/ClassFiniteness.lean :: FiniteProjectiveLatticeCat.exists_ne_zero_pairing_le','The existing positive-definite bound has coefficient n. The source bound is (4/3)^((n-1)/2), allows indefinite forms and its isotropic zero case. Neither the constant nor the hypotheses agree.','hermite')
u(137,'P/MeasureTheory/Group/GeometryOfNumbers.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/ClassFiniteness.lean','The source covolume-squared identity is taken in the Euclidean absolute-value metric associated with an indefinite form. A positive-definite or unformed Euclidean lattice formula needs this specific metric comparison.','hermite')
u(138,'A/Lattices/Valued/Mass.lean :: genusClassSet_finite','The theorem in Mass assumes positive definiteness. The source genus-finiteness corollary includes indefinite nondegenerate genera; no such general statement was identified.','classfinite')
a(139,'A/Lattices/Valued/Mass.lean :: classNumber, GenusClass','The class number is the cardinality of the existing quotient class set of a genus, under its finiteness instance. This definition does not itself establish the preceding general finiteness theorem.','mass')
u(140,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalGlobal.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean','The two specified class-number-one examples require their integral genus classifications, not just constructors for the ternary lattice or A2.','classfinite')
a(141,'A/Lattices/Valued/Mass.lean :: mass','The explicit finite family mass is the sum of reciprocal cardinalities of its orthogonal groups. Use the positive-definite hypothesis to justify finiteness of those groups, not as a hidden generalization to indefinite mass.','mass')
u(142,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/Arithmetic.lean','The Niemeier type is the locus of positive definite even unimodular rank-24 lattices; no canonical owner for that locus was identified. Constructing a particular orthogonal sum does not define its classification class.','niemeier')
u(143,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean; T/LinearAlgebra/IntegralLattice/RootLattice','No complete classification into exactly 24 rank-24 positive even unimodular isometry classes found; GitHub Niemeier query returned no Lean hits at the recorded date.','niemeier')
u(144,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean; X/SpherePacking','The source includes several Niemeier examples and uniqueness of the rootless Leech lattice. Sphere-packing optimality or an E8 model is not the Niemeier/rootless uniqueness theorem.','niemeier')
a(145,'A/Lattices/Valued/Mass.lean :: genusMass','For the positive definite context in which the finite orthogonal-group mass is defined, this is the finite sum over global isometry classes in the genus, with independence from chosen representatives.','mass')
a(146,'A/Lattices/Valued/Theta.lean :: representationNumber, thetaSeries','The series counts vectors at each integral norm using the native pairing convention. Source q/b normalization must be stated explicitly when changing the exponent; finite coefficients require positive definiteness.','mass')
u(147,'A/Lattices/Valued/Theta.lean','The unit requires nonisometric E8⊕E8 and Gamma16 to have equal theta series and the resulting flat-torus isospectral comparison. A general theta-series definition proves none of these.','mass')
u(148,'A/Lattices/Valued/DefiniteIndefinite.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/OrthogonalSummand.lean','No uniqueness theorem for the decomposition of every definite integral lattice into orthogonally indecomposable summands was identified. Root-graph connectedness and a chosen complement are not that result.','classfinite')
u(149,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/GenusInvariants.lean','The indefinite unimodular classification needs existence and uniqueness for all allowed ranks/signatures/parities and the mod-eight constraint, not just standard examples.','nikulin')
u(150,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean','The source identification of every odd unimodular rank-seven index-minus-one lattice with the specified diagonal model depends on the full indefinite classification, which is not an identified owner.','nikulin')
u(151,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean :: k3Lattice','The constructed even unimodular lattice of signature (3,19) is available, but the source asserts uniqueness among all such lattices. The constructor does not cover that classification.','nikulin')
u(152,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean','The Enriques-signature even unimodular model can be constructed as U⊕E8(-1), but the source uniqueness assertion is not supplied by that construction.','nikulin')
u(153,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean','The binary indefinite unimodular classification and the parity-dependent basis changes for matrix [[0,1],[1,a]] are not an identified full result.','nikulin')
u(154,'A/Lattices/Valued/LocalGlobal.lean; A/Lattices/Valued/EvenGluing.lean','The rank≥length+2 singleton-genus theorem for even indefinite lattices is a classification theorem, not an implication of the glue construction or SameGenus predicate.','nikulin')
u(155,'A/Lattices/Valued/Standard.lean','The examples require the singleton-genus conclusion, bounds for scaled E8/Gamma forms and unimodular summand arguments. Neither particular constructors nor the unproved general criterion closes the bundle.','nikulin')
